      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it. One more for the road. I'm looking at how these small units cluster together. In some of these agglutinative structures, the way the morphemes attach can feel almost... unpredictable or like they are following their own internal logic that's hard to map.\n\nCould you explain the concept of \"morpheme agglutination\" generally? I want to understand how these tiny, distinct units can stack up to create such specific meanings without losing their individual identities. It's a bit like seeing a bunch of small, separate parts suddenly forming a single complex object.",
